<title>JAPAN: Nippon Credit Bank shares hit limit high.</title>
<headline>Nippon Credit Bank shares hit limit high.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nippon Credit Bank Ltd shares hit their daily limit high in heavy trade on Friday afternoon.  </p>
<p>The shares surged by 50 yen, their daily limit, to touch 240 yen in the afternoon. The issue topped the list of percentage gainers on the first section of Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The trading volume was 24.180 million shares at 0515 GMT, the heaviest on the first section.</p>
<p>The bank's announcement on Thursday that it and Bankers Trust New York Corp had agreed a business tie-up, prompted traders who had sold off the shares to buy back actively, traders said.</p>
</text>
